<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
DESIGN LEDGER: printable mechanical ankle V2.1; isolated RL input, 2026-09-12.
Canonical URDF XML; source geometry: ankle_v2_printable.py, unchanged ST3215 bay.
Units SI; STL millimetres with .001 scale. Body X forward Y left Z up.
Knee/ankle frames and signs inherited from V2; knee-to-ankle 0.15989668899999998 m.
New shank mesh has knee at origin; foot mesh has ankle at origin.
Two fixed 55 g motor cases per shank; 4 g shank fixings allowance.
Printed mass uses CAD B-rep volume/inertia at 1240 * .65 kg/m3 effective density.
The .65 solid fraction estimates walls plus infill, is NOT measured slicer mass.
Foot adds 6 g tread and 10 g screws/nuts allowance. Total estimate 3.350937565 kg.
Mass calculations: cad/reviews/ankle-v2-printable/author_training_model.py and training-mass-properties.json.
Remaining links retain prior mass calibration; no whole-robot renormalization.
External box collision approximations; detailed cavities/fastener contact omitted.
Ankle +/-35 deg is a simulation assumption, not a qualified physical range.
Known lower-leg STL exporter warning remains unresolved; collision does not use that mesh.
This asset does not qualify printing, mechanical fit, strength or hardware operation.
-->
